From: Alexandr Mironov <7062352+alexandr-mironov@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] render: skip surfaces that have no texture

This one is against phoc (https://gitlab.gnome.org/World/Phosh/phoc), not
pmaports. Tested against phoc 0.56.0.

view_render_to_buffer_iterator() checks that the surface has a buffer, but not
that a texture could actually be obtained from it. wlr_surface_get_texture()
may still return NULL, and wlr_render_pass_add_texture() dereferences
options->texture right away, so the compositor takes a SIGSEGV:

  #0 wlr_render_pass_add_texture    subprojects/wlroots-0.20.x/render/pass.c:23
  #1 view_render_to_buffer_iterator src/render.c:430
  #2 surface_for_each_surface       subprojects/wlroots-0.20.x/types/wlr_compositor.c:1157
  #3 phoc_renderer_render_view_to_buffer  src/render.c:490
  #4 thumbnail_frame_handle_copy    src/phosh-private.c:450
  #9 wl_event_loop_dispatch

This is reachable from normal shell use rather than from anything exotic:
opening the overview asks phoc for window thumbnails, and a view whose texture
is not available at that moment takes down the compositor, and with it the
whole session — the user is dropped back to the greeter.

Observed repeatedly on a Xiaomi POCO X3 Pro (aarch64, mainline sm8150 kernel,
Mesa/freedreno on Adreno 640) running postmarketOS edge.

---
 src/render.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/src/render.c
+++ b/src/render.c
@@ -413,6 +413,9 @@
     return;

   texture = wlr_surface_get_texture (surface);
+  if (!texture)
+    return;
+
   phoc_view_get_geometry (data->view, &geo);
   wlr_surface_get_buffer_source_box (surface, &src_box);

